{
  "id": "salience-hypothesis",
  "term": "salience hypothesis",
  "definition": "In this packet, the salience hypothesis refers to the mortality salience idea that when a crisis makes thoughts of death more prominent, people become more motivated to seek affiliation and are more likely to conform. This conformity is described as a psychological defense that can reduce distress and negative emotion.",
